1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,400
India sells medicines to around two hundred countries.

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:06,650
That's why you hear it called the pharmacy of the world.

3
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:11,460
But open one antibiotic capsule and look at the white powder inside.

4
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:16,840
That's the actual medicine... and there's a fair chance its journey began in China.

5
00:00:16,950 --> 00:00:20,010
The rest of the capsule is just there to carry it to you.

6
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:22,640
Now think back to the Corona days.

7
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:23,710
You remember them.

8
00:00:23,740 --> 00:00:24,840
Not the lockdown yet —

9
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:26,700
this is three weeks before it.

10
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:29,010
The third of March, twenty twenty.

11
00:00:29,130 --> 00:00:29,670
In China,

12
00:00:29,670 --> 00:00:33,610
the city of Wuhan has been locked down for almost six weeks.

13
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:34,420
Here in India,

14
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:36,920
there are only a handful of cases so far.

15
00:00:37,090 --> 00:00:37,830
Delhi.

16
00:00:37,910 --> 00:00:39,900
A two-page government order goes out,

17
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:41,720
and if you run a medicine company,

18
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:43,470
your phone starts ringing.

19
00:00:43,530 --> 00:00:45,180
Thirteen medicine ingredients,

20
00:00:45,180 --> 00:00:47,000
and the medicines made from them,

21
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,340
can't leave India without a licence.

22
00:00:49,370 --> 00:00:51,210
Paracetamol is one of them.

23
00:00:52,890 --> 00:00:53,500
Wait.

24
00:00:53,590 --> 00:00:54,310
India?

25
00:00:54,470 --> 00:00:57,830
The pharmacy of the world... locking its own doors?

26
00:00:58,290 --> 00:00:59,020
Yes.

27
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:00,920
And the reason was Corona.

28
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:06,080
Wuhan sits in a Chinese province called Hubei... and the whole province was shut down.

29
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:11,270
Reports at the time said many of the ingredients on that list came from that one place.

30
00:01:11,340 --> 00:01:13,960
So here's the question I want to answer for you today.

31
00:01:14,050 --> 00:01:19,350
If India makes medicine for the world... who makes the powder inside India's medicine?

32
00:01:19,430 --> 00:01:20,530
And before you worry —

33
00:01:20,530 --> 00:01:23,160
this isn't about the quality of your medicines.

34
00:01:23,190 --> 00:01:25,710
It's about who controls the supply.

35
00:01:26,670 --> 00:01:27,670
Stay with me.

36
00:01:27,770 --> 00:01:28,930
Around minute eight,

37
00:01:28,930 --> 00:01:31,590
I'll take you to a fight India is in right now

38
00:01:31,590 --> 00:01:33,100
— in Andhra Pradesh.

39
00:01:33,290 --> 00:01:36,550
And I'll give you the date that could decide how it ends.

40
00:01:36,770 --> 00:01:39,000
First, let's give India its due.

41
00:01:39,090 --> 00:01:41,220
Because that pharmacy of the world title?

42
00:01:41,300 --> 00:01:42,690
India earned it.

43
00:01:42,950 --> 00:01:44,630
Think back to two thousand one.

44
00:01:44,740 --> 00:01:47,370
H.I.V. is killing millions in Africa.

45
00:01:47,430 --> 00:01:50,590
The medicines exist... but the Western price is around

46
00:01:50,590 --> 00:01:53,510
ten thousand dollars a year for one patient.

47
00:01:53,660 --> 00:01:55,570
Then an Indian company, Cipla,

48
00:01:55,570 --> 00:02:00,390
stands up and offers the same three-drug mix for about a dollar a day.

49
00:02:00,510 --> 00:02:01,600
One dollar.

50
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:05,610
That one offer helped change how the world priced these medicines.

51
00:02:06,590 --> 00:02:07,140
And today,

52
00:02:07,140 --> 00:02:09,940
you'll find India sells medicines abroad worth more

53
00:02:09,940 --> 00:02:12,760
than two and a half lakh crore rupees a year.

54
00:02:12,910 --> 00:02:14,900
So where's the missing piece?

55
00:02:15,100 --> 00:02:16,110
Here's the catch.

56
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:18,260
Every tablet has two parts.

57
00:02:18,290 --> 00:02:20,880
There's the powder that actually makes you better.

58
00:02:20,940 --> 00:02:23,390
The industry calls it the A.P.I. — and no,

59
00:02:23,390 --> 00:02:25,020
not the computer kind.

60
00:02:25,060 --> 00:02:26,510
Let's just call it the powder.

61
00:02:26,610 --> 00:02:30,310
And then there's everything around it... the rest of the tablet,

62
00:02:30,310 --> 00:02:32,500
the coating, the strip, the box.

63
00:02:32,530 --> 00:02:34,170
And you should be proud of this.

64
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:37,270
Indian companies are world class at that last part.

65
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:38,950
Mixing, pressing, packing,

66
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:42,490
and passing the toughest inspections on the planet.

67
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:44,010
But the powder you swallow?

68
00:02:44,060 --> 00:02:46,750
A lot of it is made somewhere else first.

69
00:02:46,780 --> 00:02:48,000
In twenty twenty-five,

70
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:53,530
India bought these powders from other countries worth around sixty-five thousand crore rupees.

71
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:55,600
And the biggest seller, by far...

72
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:56,510
China.

73
00:02:58,130 --> 00:03:01,270
And if you look at antibiotics, it gets worse.

74
00:03:01,410 --> 00:03:02,210
Niti Aayog —

75
00:03:02,210 --> 00:03:04,860
that's the government's own think tank —

76
00:03:04,860 --> 00:03:08,560
says out of every hundred rupees India spent on imported

77
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:12,360
antibiotic powder... about eighty-six went to China.

78
00:03:12,520 --> 00:03:14,800
Even your fever tablet has a China link.

79
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:17,670
Indian factories do make paracetamol powder.

80
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:19,560
But the raw chemical it's made from?

81
00:03:19,710 --> 00:03:23,810
Industry reports say a big share of that still comes from China.

82
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:25,370
So you might be thinking —

83
00:03:25,370 --> 00:03:27,160
has it always been like this?

84
00:03:27,190 --> 00:03:29,310
Did India ever make its own powder?

85
00:03:29,430 --> 00:03:30,190
It did.

86
00:03:30,310 --> 00:03:31,850
And this part of the story,

87
00:03:31,850 --> 00:03:33,860
most people have never heard.

88
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:37,480
Pimpri, near Pune.

89
00:03:37,590 --> 00:03:38,940
Nineteen fifty-four.

90
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:41,540
India has been free for less than seven years,

91
00:03:41,540 --> 00:03:44,890
and it's building a factory to make its own penicillin.

92
00:03:45,040 --> 00:03:47,670
Penicillin was the miracle drug of that time.

93
00:03:47,750 --> 00:03:48,280
Back then,

94
00:03:48,280 --> 00:03:50,750
a small cut on your hand could kill you.

95
00:03:50,890 --> 00:03:51,740
With penicillin,

96
00:03:51,740 --> 00:03:54,270
it became a few days of medicine for you.

97
00:03:56,430 --> 00:04:00,190
The government sets up a company called Hindustan Antibiotics.

98
00:04:00,220 --> 00:04:01,670
By nineteen fifty-six,

99
00:04:01,670 --> 00:04:05,190
Indian penicillin is coming out of Indian tanks.

100
00:04:05,270 --> 00:04:06,500
Just think about it.

101
00:04:06,530 --> 00:04:08,430
Picture your grandparents' India.

102
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:09,950
A young, poor country,

103
00:04:09,950 --> 00:04:15,090
growing one of the most important medicines on earth... in its own factory.

104
00:04:15,180 --> 00:04:18,310
Soon, others join in — big names you may know,

105
00:04:18,310 --> 00:04:21,040
like Alembic, Sarabhai and Ranbaxy.

106
00:04:21,190 --> 00:04:24,220
India is making its own antibiotics.

107
00:04:24,310 --> 00:04:25,850
But to see what happened next,

108
00:04:25,850 --> 00:04:27,580
you need to know one thing.

109
00:04:27,690 --> 00:04:29,950
How do you actually make penicillin?

110
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:32,810
Many medicines, like paracetamol,

111
00:04:32,810 --> 00:04:35,840
are cooked from chemicals, step by step.

112
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:37,680
Penicillin is different.

113
00:04:37,770 --> 00:04:39,380
Penicillin is grown.

114
00:04:39,610 --> 00:04:44,120
You take a special mould... a cousin of the green patches you've seen on old bread.

115
00:04:44,320 --> 00:04:46,230
You put it in a giant steel tank,

116
00:04:46,230 --> 00:04:48,320
and you feed it sugar and air.

117
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:51,650
For about a week, the tank runs day and night.

118
00:04:51,760 --> 00:04:53,040
The mould eats, grows,

119
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:55,800
and gives out penicillin into the liquid.

120
00:04:55,980 --> 00:04:58,150
And if even one stray germ gets in,

121
00:04:58,150 --> 00:05:00,290
you can lose the whole batch.

122
00:05:02,930 --> 00:05:05,610
Then you take the penicillin out and clean it.

123
00:05:05,710 --> 00:05:08,480
This first powder is called penicillin G.

124
00:05:08,650 --> 00:05:11,600
Next, it's turned into a smaller base powder.

125
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:13,490
Factories call it six A.P.A.,

126
00:05:13,490 --> 00:05:15,790
but let's just call it the base.

127
00:05:15,960 --> 00:05:18,660
From that base, factories make amoxicillin —

128
00:05:18,660 --> 00:05:21,510
the antibiotic in so many strips at home.

129
00:05:21,730 --> 00:05:23,820
Now here's the secret of this business.

130
00:05:23,950 --> 00:05:26,500
A bigger tank makes the powder cheaper.

131
00:05:26,550 --> 00:05:27,700
Much cheaper.

132
00:05:27,850 --> 00:05:28,500
Why?

133
00:05:28,660 --> 00:05:31,520
The tank must stay perfectly clean, cool,

134
00:05:31,520 --> 00:05:34,740
and full of air, every hour of every day.

135
00:05:34,890 --> 00:05:38,100
That takes a lot of power, water and steam.

136
00:05:38,300 --> 00:05:39,530
Think of a flour mill.

137
00:05:39,650 --> 00:05:43,270
A big chakki grinds each kilo cheaper than a small one.

138
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:44,380
Double your tank,

139
00:05:44,380 --> 00:05:47,710
and your costs don't double... but your output does.

140
00:05:49,750 --> 00:05:51,630
So you can guess who wins.

141
00:05:51,670 --> 00:05:54,900
The country with the biggest tanks and the cheapest power.

142
00:05:55,020 --> 00:05:58,020
And that's exactly where India's story turns.

143
00:05:58,220 --> 00:06:00,130
Now, here's what we got wrong.

144
00:06:00,310 --> 00:06:00,890
For years,

145
00:06:00,890 --> 00:06:04,810
India's government allowed only a few companies to make penicillin,

146
00:06:04,810 --> 00:06:06,680
and only in small amounts.

147
00:06:06,780 --> 00:06:09,860
So our plants stayed too small to be cheap.

148
00:06:10,390 --> 00:06:12,540
Meanwhile, in the nineteen nineties,

149
00:06:12,540 --> 00:06:15,390
China went all in on medicine ingredients.

150
00:06:15,490 --> 00:06:18,180
It built huge plants, in huge drug parks,

151
00:06:18,180 --> 00:06:20,700
with cheap power and cheap water.

152
00:06:20,790 --> 00:06:24,030
Its factories also faced looser pollution rules.

153
00:06:24,150 --> 00:06:30,460
And then cheap Chinese penicillin flooded the world market... at prices nobody else could match.

154
00:06:30,780 --> 00:06:32,490
Now remember this one number.

155
00:06:32,640 --> 00:06:33,830
Nineteen ninety-one —

156
00:06:33,830 --> 00:06:36,270
the year India opened up its economy.

157
00:06:36,430 --> 00:06:39,640
Of all the medicine powder India bought from outside,

158
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:42,060
China sold less than one per cent.

159
00:06:42,390 --> 00:06:43,670
Less than one.

160
00:06:43,960 --> 00:06:45,120
Then, one by one,

161
00:06:45,120 --> 00:06:48,200
the Indian penicillin plants went quiet.

162
00:06:49,980 --> 00:06:51,540
Hindustan Antibiotics.

163
00:06:51,610 --> 00:06:52,400
Stopped.

164
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:54,090
I.D.P.L.

165
00:06:54,130 --> 00:06:54,950
Stopped.

166
00:06:55,650 --> 00:06:56,430
Torrent.

167
00:06:56,470 --> 00:06:57,460
Ranbaxy.

168
00:06:57,490 --> 00:06:58,410
Sarabhai.

169
00:06:58,440 --> 00:06:59,270
Stopped.

170
00:06:59,910 --> 00:07:01,410
And the last one standing...

171
00:07:01,530 --> 00:07:02,270
Alembic.

172
00:07:02,470 --> 00:07:03,290
Stopped.

173
00:07:04,960 --> 00:07:06,320
By about twenty twenty,

174
00:07:06,320 --> 00:07:10,190
India was importing all of that base powder for amoxicillin.

175
00:07:10,280 --> 00:07:11,880
Every last kilo.

176
00:07:12,040 --> 00:07:13,620
Remember that one per cent?

177
00:07:13,650 --> 00:07:15,780
That was for all medicine powder.

178
00:07:15,880 --> 00:07:16,120
Now,

179
00:07:16,120 --> 00:07:19,230
if you look at just antibiotic powder today...

180
00:07:19,290 --> 00:07:22,100
China's share is around eighty-six per cent.

181
00:07:22,290 --> 00:07:25,620
Niti Aayog estimates Chinese powder costs thirty-five to

182
00:07:25,620 --> 00:07:28,710
forty per cent less than powder made in India.

183
00:07:28,830 --> 00:07:30,680
So tell me — if you ran a company,

184
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:32,610
would you build a plant here?

185
00:07:32,830 --> 00:07:33,830
That's the trap.

186
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:36,220
You can't compete without a big plant.

187
00:07:36,250 --> 00:07:40,490
And you can't risk a big plant... when one price war can wipe it out.

188
00:07:40,590 --> 00:07:42,540
For years, that trap held.

189
00:07:42,680 --> 00:07:43,840
Then Corona came —

190
00:07:43,840 --> 00:07:46,500
and India had to lock its own doors.

191
00:07:47,530 --> 00:07:48,260
And this time,

192
00:07:48,260 --> 00:07:51,170
the central government decided to break the trap.

193
00:07:51,820 --> 00:07:54,820
It launched a scheme to pay companies extra for making

194
00:07:54,820 --> 00:07:57,840
forty-one of these missing ingredients in India.

195
00:07:58,010 --> 00:08:01,440
Nearly seven thousand crore rupees, set aside.

196
00:08:01,630 --> 00:08:04,650
And one company took the biggest bet of all.

197
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:08,300
Kakinada, Andhra Pradesh.

198
00:08:08,550 --> 00:08:10,700
On the coast, a new plant goes up,

199
00:08:10,700 --> 00:08:12,350
built by Aurobindo Pharma,

200
00:08:12,350 --> 00:08:14,660
through its unit called Lyfius.

201
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:17,750
Inside are the giant tanks I just told you about.

202
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:22,080
The company says it cost around two thousand five hundred crore rupees,

203
00:08:22,080 --> 00:08:26,760
and it's built to make fifteen thousand tonnes of penicillin G every year.

204
00:08:26,890 --> 00:08:29,960
In twenty twenty-four, the tanks start running.

205
00:08:30,180 --> 00:08:33,020
For the first time in more than ten years...

206
00:08:33,050 --> 00:08:36,160
India is growing its own penicillin again.

207
00:08:36,360 --> 00:08:37,990
But you know the trap.

208
00:08:38,110 --> 00:08:40,070
Even with Indian penicillin ready,

209
00:08:40,070 --> 00:08:43,010
cheap imports were still waiting at the port.

210
00:08:43,120 --> 00:08:44,860
So on the twenty-ninth of January,

211
00:08:44,860 --> 00:08:47,520
twenty twenty-six, the government stepped in.

212
00:08:47,610 --> 00:08:49,990
It set a minimum price at the border.

213
00:08:50,050 --> 00:08:54,920
If penicillin powder comes in cheaper than about two thousand two hundred rupees a kilo,

214
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:56,980
it now needs a special licence.

215
00:08:57,030 --> 00:09:00,300
The same rule covers amoxicillin and its base powder.

216
00:09:00,350 --> 00:09:02,030
Think of it as a shield.

217
00:09:02,060 --> 00:09:04,270
It gives the new Indian plant breathing room,

218
00:09:04,270 --> 00:09:06,880
while it grows big enough to stand on its own.

219
00:09:06,990 --> 00:09:09,000
And in September twenty twenty-six,

220
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:11,060
after the Kakinada plant complained,

221
00:09:11,060 --> 00:09:14,110
the government also started checking whether China is

222
00:09:14,110 --> 00:09:16,930
selling penicillin here below a fair price.

223
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,570
But that shield has an end date.

224
00:09:19,690 --> 00:09:23,720
It runs for one year... until January twenty twenty-seven.

225
00:09:24,300 --> 00:09:25,850
That's the date to watch.

226
00:09:25,980 --> 00:09:28,260
Will Kakinada be strong enough by then?

227
00:09:28,380 --> 00:09:30,400
Or will the shield get extended?

228
00:09:30,620 --> 00:09:33,310
And here's the balance the government has to strike.

229
00:09:33,460 --> 00:09:37,610
Protect the Indian plant... without making your antibiotics costlier.

230
00:09:37,810 --> 00:09:39,420
And it's not just penicillin.

231
00:09:39,450 --> 00:09:44,000
Companies have already put more than five thousand crore rupees into this scheme.

232
00:09:44,030 --> 00:09:45,420
And there's more coming.

233
00:09:45,450 --> 00:09:48,430
Three giant bulk drug parks are being built —

234
00:09:48,430 --> 00:09:49,160
in Gujarat,

235
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:52,500
in Himachal Pradesh... and one at Nakkapalli.

236
00:09:52,570 --> 00:09:53,890
Yes, you heard right —

237
00:09:53,890 --> 00:09:55,640
that's in Andhra Pradesh too,

238
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:58,220
the same state as the Kakinada plant.

239
00:09:58,420 --> 00:09:59,780
Let me be honest with you.

240
00:09:59,860 --> 00:10:02,220
None of those parks is up and running yet.

241
00:10:02,250 --> 00:10:04,550
And China has a thirty-year head start,

242
00:10:04,550 --> 00:10:07,320
and makes far more penicillin than we do.

243
00:10:07,380 --> 00:10:09,090
So has India won?

244
00:10:09,170 --> 00:10:10,020
Not yet.

245
00:10:10,050 --> 00:10:11,910
But it's back in the fight.

246
00:10:11,950 --> 00:10:13,170
So here's the lesson.

247
00:10:13,230 --> 00:10:15,240
If you only master the last step,

248
00:10:15,240 --> 00:10:19,120
you're only as strong as whoever controls the step before.

249
00:10:19,190 --> 00:10:20,170
And the cost?

250
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:21,860
You saw it in the Corona days.

251
00:10:21,890 --> 00:10:23,990
When one province in China shut down,

252
00:10:23,990 --> 00:10:27,270
the pharmacy of the world had to lock its own doors.

253
00:10:27,300 --> 00:10:29,040
But here's the reality today.

254
00:10:29,070 --> 00:10:30,830
India has the scientists.

255
00:10:30,860 --> 00:10:32,430
It has the factories.

256
00:10:32,460 --> 00:10:35,630
And now, it's growing its own penicillin again.

257
00:10:35,710 --> 00:10:37,380
So what does this mean for you?

258
00:10:37,470 --> 00:10:40,650
Keep taking your medicines exactly as your doctor says.

259
00:10:40,680 --> 00:10:42,700
Nothing in this story changes that.

260
00:10:42,820 --> 00:10:44,890
But the next time you take an antibiotic,

261
00:10:44,890 --> 00:10:46,750
think about that white powder.

262
00:10:46,790 --> 00:10:50,280
There's a fair chance part of its journey began in China.

263
00:10:50,310 --> 00:10:55,650
And if the plant in Kakinada wins... the next one might start right here in India.

264
00:10:56,170 --> 00:10:58,770
Medicines aren't the only missing piece.

265
00:10:58,910 --> 00:11:01,490
India writes software for the whole world.

266
00:11:01,520 --> 00:11:06,710
So why is India's own A.I. still so far behind America's and China's?

267
